## Why the draft test flakes

Before writing anything, three separate defects — the midnight one is only the most visible:

1. **It reads the real clock twice.** `dueDate(new Date())` and `addDays(new Date(), 30)` are two different instants. Straddle midnight and the second call is a day later — the flake you saw.
2. **It compares two different instants even when it doesn't straddle midnight.** `toEqual` on `Date` compares exact milliseconds, so the microseconds between the two `new Date()` calls make this fail on a slow machine (or CI under load). It isn't only a midnight problem.
3. **It asserts the implementation against itself.** If `src/billing/due.js` computes the due date with `addDays`, the expectation is produced by the same helper, so the test still passes when `addDays` is wrong. It can't catch the bug it exists for.

